          { stage: "Stage 1 (Avoid)", power: "N/A", notes: "Tuning the N45 is universally discouraged. While it lacks Valvetronic, the core engine architecture is incredibly fragile. The cost of a simple remap is far better spent on preventative maintenance (timing chains).", zeroToHundred: "N/A", hundredToTwoHundred: "N/A" },
          { stage: "Stage 2 (Avoid)", power: "N/A", notes: "Do not attempt to tune an N45 with exhaust or intake modifications. The engine is designed purely for low emissions and efficiency, not high RPM breathing.", zeroToHundred: "N/A", hundredToTwoHundred: "N/A" },
          { stage: "Stage 3 (Engine Swap)", power: "190+ hp", notes: "The ultimate 'tune' for an N45-equipped E46 is removing the disastrous 4-cylinder entirely and dropping in an M52TU or M54 6-cylinder engine (e.g., swapping to a 325i or 330i spec). It cures all reliability issues and transforms the car.", zeroToHundred: "7.2s (With M54B30 swap)", hundredToTwoHundred: "18.0s" }
